{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109263","id":2715594426,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6h3K66","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109263","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109263.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109263.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109263","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109263/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109263/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109263/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a8d9c628075a7de90c55b9db7cae6e9435959454","number":109263,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Add a `@final` annotation for methods and classes","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds the `@final` annotation, which can be used on Methods and Classes to mark them as non-extensible. For classes, that means no class may `extend` that class. For methods, it means that no subclass may override that method.\r\n\r\nThis is a continuation of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107722\r\n\r\nThe differences from the former PR are as follows:\r\n1. `is_final()` is not exposed to GDScript. This matches with the fact that we did not expose `is_abstract()` to GDS.\r\n2. `@final` is only usable on _named_ classes (and not script files).\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10500\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1311\r\n\r\n___\r\nTo address some broader discussion around the usage of `@final` in GDS:\r\n\r\nPer @dalexeev:\r\n> Personally, I would prefer virtual/override over final.\r\n\r\nVirtual, Override, and Final have different behaviors and all work concurrently. Introduction of `@final` does not preclude introduction of either of the other two. On a virtual method, final means no further methods may override it. You would still want a `@final` annotation even in a non-virtual-by-default model. Hence this opinion has no impact on this change.\r\n\r\nFurther on that note, GDS already has virtual-by-default semantics **as a core language feature**. Changing that, at this point in the language, is a non-starter.\r\n\r\nPer @HolonProduction:\r\n> So a final class that extends from Node should not be attachable to Node2D IMO\r\n\r\nI don't know enough about GD's serialization to comment on this effectively. I'm not sure I follow how this would improve the security of serialization.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwOD